- implementation/core/src/re_frame/frame.cljc ~2013 (swap-partition!'s exact write);
- implementation/machines/src/re_frame/machines/timer.cljc ~943 (after-cancel-fx);
- implementation/machines/src/re_frame/machines/lifecycle_fx/spawn.cljc ~1367.
And implementation/core/src/re_frame/late_bind/directory.cljc, the :epoch/on-frame-destroyed row (~657), still says "a stale A that lost to a claimed same-id B" and "a same-id B claiming the stores". Step 10 runs while the destroy still holds the id.
Check each writer site by site at tip, reading frame.cljc's destroy request path and the router's drain. Where a successor really cannot be seated, restate the comment to the present reason. Where the guard it describes is still needed for another reason (a tool write outside any drain, or the late drain-interrupted report), keep it and say which. If a guard the comment justifies turns out to be dead code, say so in the PR and stop there: deleting it is a separate bead. Comments and docstrings only.

